{#
    FORK (FORK.md): panels above the search results, each loaded by a lazy
    frame of its own once the list is on screen. See ForkSearchInsightController
    for why they are separate.

    Only on the first page of a search with words in it: a page further down is
    somebody reading the list, not asking a question.

    The panels' links open their mail the way a row of the list does
    (mail--mail-pane#open). A plain link navigated the lazy frame it sat in:
    Turbo moves only the CONTENTS of the frame that arrives into this
    placeholder, so the `target="_top"` written on it was never read, and the
    page went blank until a reload. The placeholders say `_top` themselves for
    anything else that is clicked in them.
#}
<li class="border-b border-line" data-fork-search-insight>
    <turbo-frame id="fork-search-trips" src="{{ path('app_fork_search_trips', { q: q }) }}" loading="lazy" target="_top"></turbo-frame>
    {% if has_results %}
        <turbo-frame id="fork-search-best" src="{{ path('app_fork_search_best', { q: q }) }}" loading="lazy" target="_top"></turbo-frame>
        <turbo-frame id="fork-search-answer" src="{{ path('app_fork_search_answer', { q: q }) }}" loading="lazy" target="_top">
            <div class="px-4 py-2.5 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-faint" data-fork-answer-state="loading">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles animate-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'search.fork_insight.loading'|trans({}, 'fork') }}
            </div>
        </turbo-frame>
    {% endif %}
</li>
